  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Emergency Response to Conflict and Climate Shock Affected Internally Displaced Populations and Communities in Northern Mozambique &#x2013; Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique faces a triple humanitarian crisis with conflict, reoccurring disasters related to natural hazards and climactic shocks, and the impact of the coronavirus becoming increasingly complex. While the multisectoral response in Northern Mozambique has increased, the needs remain high. There is an urgent need to scale up in the listed areas to ensure adequate response to the needs of those affected by the conflict in Northern Mozambique while also ensuring capacity to respond to sudden onset climatic shocks which commonly occur during Mozambique&apos;s annual cyclone season from November to May and affect coastal and low-lying areas. 
 
In response, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) provides a lifesaving multi-sectoral response and mitigation assistance for displaced people and host communities in northern Mozambique. Contributing to humanitarian coordination, IOM continues the implementation of the Displacement Tracking Matrix and maintains leadership positions in cluster coordination mechanisms, particularly for the Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) and Shelter clusters. Moreover, IOM is strengthening its provision of protection, mental health and psychosocial support, shelter and settlements, CCCM, and water, sanitation and hygiene services.</narrative>
  </description>
